  "full_text": "So, God said the 11th commandment is not to litter. Someone left some bread, and it made a mess of crumbs. You know, I'm kind of a frustration for the city they're trying to organize, and I'm not really doing anything wrong, but on the other hand, I'm screwing up all their plans, because it's a big system, and if one breaks down, the whole system breaks down. And anyway, so... In the daytime, there's sparrows that eat little bits of food. But like at nighttime, these rats come out and eat. And so like this litter, this bread is particularly crummy. It was like charity bread. I went ahead and had some because it was like, it was kind of going to go to waste. And anyway, and I made a mess. And that can wear out your welcome. And also it can cause rats. And also God said not to litter. And anyway, so. God the Bible says deeds are evil are done in darkness and You know Camelot It never rains till after sundown Came a lot. Maybe if I had a lot of kids it would be marked in trolls or something. I don't know but uh interesting",
